From e27818e4663a4f16ce1467df269ab0cac4fa8ccb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:33:42 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): bound the SSH keep-alive to the warm set so
 one-off dials stop pinning remote backends [daveey]

Desktop main held an idle-exit-blocking /api/ws keep-alive (#106935) on every
published SSH-isolated scope until teardown, so a single sweep over a host's
profiles kept every one of those backends alive for the whole Desktop session
(9 serve --isolated on the mini, 4 outside the prewarm set, no renderer client,
holding the BB memory gate at WARN).

The keep-alive now stays only on the primary, bare/local/non-SSH scopes, the
default profile, the prewarm targets (default + recent cap 4) and scopes dialled
for use in the last 30 min (ssh-keepalive-hold.ts, reconciled every 15 s).
Other scopes just lose that socket: tunnel and pool entry stay, a renderer
socket or running turn still keeps the backend up, and the dispatch probe
redials one that idle-exited. Post-resume sweeps no longer rebuild a dead scope
outside that set. Warm-set wiring moved to remote-warm-set.ts (main.ts shrinks).
